/* ---------------- Sentence structures & expressions ---------------- */
col({id:'struct-w2', cat:'structures', name:'Writing Task 2 Sentence Structures', icon:'pen-tool', level:'B2–C1',
desc:'Reusable sentence patterns for introductions, arguments, examples and conclusions.',
words:`It is widely believed that …||structure|Nhiều người tin rằng …|Introduces a common opinion, often one you will discuss or challenge.|It is widely believed that university education should be free.
There is no doubt that …||structure|Không còn nghi ngờ gì rằng …|States something you are certain about; use it sparingly.|There is no doubt that technology has transformed education.
While it is true that …, I would argue that …||structure|Mặc dù đúng là …, tôi cho rằng …|Concedes one point, then gives your own position.|While it is true that cars are convenient, I would argue that they cause more problems than they solve.
One of the main reasons why … is that …||structure|Một trong những lý do chính khiến … là …|Introduces a key reason in a body paragraph.|One of the main reasons why people move to cities is that wages are higher.
This is because …||structure|Điều này là bởi vì …|Explains the previous sentence.|Many young people struggle to buy homes. This is because prices have risen faster than wages.
As a result, … / Consequently, …||structure|Kết quả là … / Do đó …|Shows a result or effect.|Fewer people cycle to work. As a result, traffic congestion has worsened.
It could be argued that …||structure|Có thể lập luận rằng …|Presents an idea cautiously, often the opposing view.|It could be argued that exams do not measure real ability.
From my perspective, …||structure|Theo quan điểm của tôi, …|Gives your opinion in a formal way.|From my perspective, the benefits of tourism outweigh the drawbacks.
In order to …, governments should …||structure|Để …, chính phủ nên …|Proposes a solution with a clear purpose.|In order to reduce obesity, governments should tax sugary drinks.
…, which means that …||structure|…, điều đó có nghĩa là …|Adds a consequence to a whole idea.|Many graduates cannot find jobs, which means that they have to move abroad.
The more …, the more …||structure|Càng … càng …|Shows two things changing together.|The more time children spend online, the less they exercise.
Not only does … but it also …||structure|Không những … mà còn …|Emphasises two related points using inversion.|Not only does public transport reduce pollution, but it also saves money.
A case in point is …||structure|Một ví dụ điển hình là …|Introduces a specific example.|Some countries have successfully reduced car use. A case in point is the Netherlands.
On the one hand, … On the other hand, …||structure|Một mặt … Mặt khác …|Compares two sides of an issue.|On the one hand, working from home saves time. On the other hand, it can be isolating.
Despite the fact that …, …||structure|Mặc dù thực tế là …, …|Contrasts two ideas in one sentence.|Despite the fact that smoking is dangerous, many teenagers still start.
… is likely to lead to …||structure|… có khả năng dẫn đến …|Predicts a consequence with appropriate caution.|Cutting school budgets is likely to lead to larger class sizes.
It is essential that … (should) …||structure|Điều thiết yếu là … (nên) …|Stresses a necessary action; the verb stays in the base form.|It is essential that every child learn to swim.
Were it not for …, …||structure|Nếu không có …, …|A formal inverted conditional for emphasis.|Were it not for vaccines, many more children would die each year.
There is a growing tendency for … to …||structure|Ngày càng có xu hướng … làm …|Describes a trend in society.|There is a growing tendency for couples to have children later in life.
In conclusion, while …, I firmly believe that …||structure|Tóm lại, mặc dù …, tôi tin chắc rằng …|Restates your position in the conclusion.|In conclusion, while technology has some drawbacks, I firmly believe that its benefits are greater.`});

col({id:'speak-expr', cat:'structures', name:'Natural Speaking Expressions', icon:'mic', level:'B1–B2',
desc:'Phrases for giving opinions, buying thinking time and extending answers in Parts 1–3.',
words:`To be honest, …||expression|Thành thật mà nói, …|Gives a sincere, personal answer.|To be honest, I'm not a big fan of spicy food.
I'd say that …||expression|Tôi cho rằng …|A softer way to give an opinion.|I'd say that my hometown is quite peaceful.
It depends on …||expression|Còn tùy vào …|Shows that the answer changes with the situation.|It depends on the weather, really.
That's a tricky question, but …||expression|Đó là câu hỏi khó, nhưng …|Buys thinking time before an abstract answer.|That's a tricky question, but I think money matters less than people think.
Off the top of my head, …||expression|Nghĩ ngay ra thì …|Answers without much preparation.|Off the top of my head, I'd say about twenty times.
I'm not really into …||expression|Tôi không thực sự thích …|Says politely that you don't enjoy something.|I'm not really into horror films.
I'm a big fan of …||expression|Tôi rất thích …|Says you really like something.|I'm a big fan of street food.
As far as I know, …||expression|Theo như tôi biết, …|Gives information you are not completely sure about.|As far as I know, the museum is free on Sundays.
What I mean is …||expression|Ý tôi là …|Clarifies or rephrases your idea.|What I mean is that people rarely talk face to face any more.
The main reason is that …||expression|Lý do chính là …|Gives a clear reason.|The main reason is that it's close to my office.
For instance, …||expression|Ví dụ, …|Introduces an example to extend an answer.|For instance, last summer I went camping with my cousins.
I used to …, but these days …||expression|Tôi từng …, nhưng dạo này …|Contrasts past and present habits.|I used to play football a lot, but these days I mostly go to the gym.
I suppose …||expression|Tôi đoán là …|Gives a tentative opinion.|I suppose it's because people are busier now.
It's not something I've thought about much, but …||expression|Tôi chưa nghĩ nhiều về điều đó, nhưng …|Handles an unexpected question naturally.|It's not something I've thought about much, but I'd probably choose the beach.
If I had the chance, I would …||expression|Nếu có cơ hội, tôi sẽ …|Talks about a hypothetical wish.|If I had the chance, I would travel around South America.
Looking back, …||expression|Nhìn lại, …|Reflects on the past.|Looking back, it was the best decision I ever made.
One thing that stands out is …||expression|Một điều nổi bật là …|Highlights a memorable detail in Part 2.|One thing that stands out is how friendly the locals were.
That reminds me of …||expression|Điều đó làm tôi nhớ đến …|Links the question to a personal story.|That reminds me of a trip I took to Da Lat.
On the whole, …||expression|Nhìn chung, …|Sums up your overall view.|On the whole, I think the changes have been positive.
I couldn't agree more.||expression|Tôi hoàn toàn đồng ý.|Shows strong agreement.|I couldn't agree more — public transport should be cheaper.`});

